oofem.out
Leonhardt and Walther shear beam no. 5, plane stress, CDPM2 crack band, bond-slip, reinforcement as frame (lattice2d)
NonLinearStatic nmsteps 1 nsteps 1 profileopt 1 nmodules 1 lstype 4 smtype 8 contextoutputstep 1000
nsteps 195 rtolv 1.e-3 stiffMode 2 maxiter 100000 reqiterations 100000 controllmode 0 psi 0.0 hpcmode 2 hpc 2 15 2 hpcw 1 -1 steplength 1.e-5 minsteplength 1.e-5 donotfixload lstype 4 smtype 8 manrmsteps 10
vtkxml primvars 1 1 cellvars 4 1 4 13 27 tstep_step 5 domain_all
domain 2dplanestress
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_output {15 4}
3 4 2 0 1
SimpleCS 1 thick 0.19
latticecs 2 material 3 shape 1 radius 0.018385 area 1.06186e-3 iz 4.4863e-8
interfacecs 3 material 4
con2dpm 1 d 0 E 30.483e9 n 0.2 talpha 0. wf 59.373e-6 fc 28.5e6 ft 2.247e6 hp 0.01 yieldtol 1.e-6 asoft 15. stype 2 kinit 0.3 ecc 0.518 efc 3.e-5 ahard 8.e-2 bhard 3.3e-3 chard 2. dhard 1.e-6 dilation 0.85
isole 2 d 0 n 0.3 e 200.e9 talpha 0.
latticeframeelastic 3 d 0 e 200.e9 n 0.3 talpha 0.
linkslip 4 kn 4.53e10 kl 4.53e13 type 2 t0 11.32e6 s1 1.e-3 s2 2.e-3 s3 8.5e-3 tf 4.53e6 alpha 0.4
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 prescribedvalue 0.0
Nodalload 2 loadTimeFunction 1 components 2 0.0 1.0
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.0

# symmetry plane x = 1.275: u_x = 0
vertex 4 5
nodeprop bc 2 1 0

curve 4
nodeprop bc 2 1 0

# support: centre of bottom plate, u_y = 0
vertex 12
nodeprop bc 2 0 1

# load: centre of top plate
vertex 15
nodeprop load 1 2

# concrete
patch 1 2
elemprop crossSect 1 mat 1
triatype trplanestress2d

# steel plates
patch 3 4
elemprop crossSect 1 mat 2
triatype trplanestress2d

# reinforcement 2 x d26: frame elements (lattice2d, u, v and rotation per
# node) on ordinary nodes. Without gpCoords, lattice2d takes the element
# midpoint as integration point. The circular latticecs gives the area of the
# two bars (radius 0.018385); iz is the moment of inertia of two 26 mm bars,
# half that of one circle with the same area. The duplicate tool (oofem fork,
# tools/duplicate) then
#   - adds a duplicated, fully hanging node at the position of each bar node
#     (it follows the host concrete element), and
#   - joins each pair with a bondlink2dtruss (crossSect 3, mat 4: linkslip):
#     bond-slip law along the bar, lateral stiffness kl across it, as in
#     cdpm2-bondslip-2d. The link uses only u and v, so the rotation of the
#     bar node is not tied to the concrete; it is carried by the frame.
curve 12
elemprop crossSect 2 mat 3
edgetype lattice2d

# bar end at the symmetry plane: u_x = 0 and rotation = 0 (the bar no longer
# follows the concrete in x, so it needs its own symmetry condition)
vertex 10
nodeprop dofidmask 3 1 2 6 bc 3 1 0 1

###### Used for Extractor
###
#%BEGIN_CHECK%
#LOADLEVEL
#DOFMAN  number 4 dof 2 type d
#DOFMAN  number 15 dof 2 type d
#%END_CHECK%
